# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machines this repo is developed on, so
# without these rules Git rewrites the Gradle wrapper script to CRLF on the
# next checkout. `./gradlew` then dies from Git Bash and from any Linux CI
# with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" - an error that reads like a broken
# toolchain rather than a line-ending problem, which is why it costs an hour.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no repo-wide `text=auto`, because renormalising every
# existing file would churn the other developer's working tree for no gain.

gradlew     text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Never let Git touch these.
*.jar  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.apk  binary
*.keystore binary
